q3lmUZ1LfBrI2rcdwtMCqpkj_fZNdzRQWZqH4NQoL1NxunIfTDEMy2lpFCryeI62sHGe0WhUvj1zcXj6Xd9FpTH512SrY2Lsgt8zAQjSDfGB9wM83q_WOl-a-XItDCiLqy15XRUk-hjhij2L8S4nl1Lm22T2-8Wzbuqdv4QPpuy1cpWwj5kEnv6z4kH_0PGM67iE8ZEW_67Jk1\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Creating initial skill skeleton**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_69zh17ttzEQpLvXAzce9GJDp|fc_0b8aa40eb7d5cf320169a6d60a7af88191a31d8916a32326e6","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\吗喽\\.openclaw\\workspace\\skills\\web-unit-testbook\\SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: web-unit-testbook\ndescription: Generate web page unit test books from detailed design Excel files, embedded images/OCR text, LWC/Apex source code, and a user-provided Excel template. Use when user asks to read design docs, extract field/API/check rules, parse code branches and data bindings, generate test cases, and fill a unit test book template (.xlsx).\n---\n\n# Web Unit Test Book Generator\n\nBuild and run a deterministic pipeline for unit test book generation.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Parse design Excel into `design_rules.json`.\n2. Parse LWC/Apex code into `code_rules.json`.\n3. Merge rules and generate markdown spec + normalized case JSON.\n4. Fill the user template workbook and export final test book.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Design workbook (`.xlsx`) with field definitions, API names, check notes, optional screenshots.\n- Code folder or zip with LWC/Apex files.\n- Unit test template workbook (`.xlsx`).\n\n## Commands\n\nRun from this skill directory.\n\n```powershell\npython scripts/parse_design_excel.py --input <design.xlsx> --out design_rules.json --ocr-lang jpn+eng\npython scripts/extract_code_rules.py --src <code_dir_or_zip> --out code_rules.json\npython scripts/generate_high_precision.py --design design_rules.json --code code_rules.json --out-md UnitTestSpec_HighPrecision.md --out-cases cases.json\npython scripts/export_to_excel.py --template <template.xlsx> --cases cases.json --out 単体試験書_WF001.xlsx\n```\n\nOr run one-shot:\n\n```powershell\npython scripts/run_pipeline.py --design <design.xlsx> --code <code_dir_or_zip> --template <template.xlsx> --outdir out\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- OCR is optional: install Tesseract and pass `--ocr-lang`.\n- If template headers are unknown, script performs best-effort column mapping by keyword.\n- Keep all output artifacts in one run directory for traceability.\n\n## Output Artifacts\n\n- `design_rules.json`\n- `code_rules.json`\n- `cases.json`\n- `UnitTestSpec_HighPrecision.md`\n- `単体試験書_*.xlsx`\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\吗喽\\\\.openclaw\\\\workspace\\\\skills\\\\web-unit-testbook\\\\SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: web-unit-testbook\\ndescription: Generate web page unit test books from detailed design Excel files, embedded images/OCR text, LWC/Apex source code, and a user-provided Excel template. Use when user asks to read design docs, extract field/API/check rules, parse code branches and data bindings, generate test cases, and fill a unit test book template (.xlsx).\\n---\\n\\n# Web Unit Test Book Generator\\n\\nBuild and run a deterministic pipeline for unit test book generation.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Parse design Excel into `design_rules.json`.\\n2. Parse LWC/Apex code into `code_rules.json`.\\n3. Merge rules and generate markdown spec + normalized case JSON.\\n4. Fill the user template workbook and export final test book.\\n\\n## Inputs\\n\\n- Design workbook (`.xlsx`) with field definitions, API names, check notes, optional screenshots.\\n- Code folder or zip with LWC/Apex files.\\n- Unit test template workbook (`.xlsx`).\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\nRun from this skill directory.\\n\\n```powershell\\npython scripts/parse_design_excel.py --input <design.xlsx> --out design_rules.json --ocr-lang jpn+eng\\npython scripts/extract_code_rules.py --src <code_dir_or_zip> --out code_rules.json\\npython scripts/generate_high_precision.py --design design_rules.json --code code_rules.json --out-md UnitTestSpec_HighPrecision.md --out-cases cases.json\\npython scripts/export_to_excel.py --template <template.xlsx> --cases cases.json --out 単体試験書_WF001.xlsx\\n```\\n\\nOr run one-shot:\\n\\n```powershell\\npython scripts/run_pipeline.py --design <design.xlsx> --code <code_dir_or_zip> --template <template.xlsx> --outdir out\\n```\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- OCR is optional: install Tesseract and pass `--ocr-lang`.\\n- If template headers are unknown, script performs best-effort column mapping by keyword.\\n- Keep all output artifacts in one run directory for traceability.\\n\\n## Output Artifacts\\n\\n- `design_rules.json`\\n- `code_rules.json`\\n- `cases.json`\\n- `UnitTestSpec_HighPrecision.md`\\n- `単体試験書_*.xlsx`\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.3-codex","usage":{"input":164,"output":698,"cacheRead":24448,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25310,"cost":{"input":0.000287,"output":0.009772,"cacheRead":0.0042784,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0143374}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772541452889}}
